-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"wontfix","close_reason":"Operator decision (2026-11-22): the rotated-out op-cert key 61689bf468f5 will not be revoked; trusted_environments.yaml keeps revoked_at_log_position null.","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision (2026-11-19 PST): keep 61689bf468f5 unrevoked.\n\nReasons:\n- The key was rotated on 2026-09-07 as part of the routine rotation sweep in auspicial-wily-warbler (899f-f964-327c-4c47). That sweep listed it among the externally anchored secrets; it was not rotated because of a compromise.\n- No evidence shows the key left the production op-cert environment's control, so it still identifies that environment.\n- Revoking it would only invalidate a legitimate identity.\n\nThe operator also stated that op-cert keys should not be hardcoded in the repository. That direction is tracked separately. No change to `trusted_environments.yaml` is made under this ticket.","timestamp":1795110116292947880},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Related: epic nonblack-brigandish-guillemot removes `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` (story prosaic-visionary-basilisk), so there will be no repo pin entry to revoke. The operator's decision lists the rotated-out key 61689bf468f5 (`nava-opcert-prod`, env 9f1c8e42) among the 3 keys in the MCP server's new deployment trust list (story unequaled-sincere-firefly). Untrusting it later means removing it from that list. No change made to this ticket's status.","timestamp":1795112792516877904}],"completion_expectation":"disposition","created_at":1795051401864018625,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ad5b7b6d-4e55-4b23-bb35-09892d70af45","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"df01-290f-89a2-4ce8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` (origin/main) pins two keys for op-cert environment 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65:\n- `nava-opcert-prod`, sha256 blob prefix 61689bf468f5, `added_at_log_position` 1784078198455948001-… (2026-07-14 PDT), `revoked_at_log_position: null`.\n- `nava-opcert-prod rotated-20260907`, prefix 6e2a8414bf53, added 1788820816306746425-… (2026-09-07 PDT), added by 665d1d04801.\n\nThe first key was rotated out on 2026-09-07 but is still unrevoked, so it is still trusted for every position after that date. On the tickets history, the last authorship signature it made is at 1788820609355938280 (2026-09-07 15:36:49 PDT), just before the rotated key was added. The last op-cert signature it made has not been checked.\n\nRevoking it is a trust-config change, so it is the operator's decision. Discovered while working starving-sphalerite-skua, where the operator chose to trust environment keys as authorship signers, era-scoped by these same fields. An unrevoked rotated key widens that trust as well.\n\n## Decision needed\nWhether to set `revoked_at_log_position` for the 61689bf468f5 record, and at which position. One candidate is 1788820816306746425-e8951143-944f-4b77-8668-0449b29cfd40, the rotated key's add position.\n\n## Decision (recorded 2026-11-19 PST)\nThe operator decided to keep 61689bf468f5 unrevoked; the decision and its reasons are in the 2026-11-19 ticket comment (routine rotation in auspicial-wily-warbler, not a compromise; no evidence the key left the production op-cert environment's control; revoking would invalidate a legitimate identity). No revocation lands, so this ticket changes no repository file. The operator's separate direction that op-cert keys should not be hardcoded in the repository is tracked elsewhere.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] [non-codebase] The operator's decision on 61689bf468f5 (keep it unrevoked, with reasons) is recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n  provenance: environment=rebar tickets store; principal=operator; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the evidence is the operator's 2026-11-19 PST decision comment on this ticket, read back with show_ticket.\n- [x] No revocation lands: `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` on origin/main still carries `revoked_at_log_position: null` for the `nava-opcert-prod` record (blob prefix 61689bf468f5), and no change to that file is made under this ticket.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1795378475295108001,"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change: the operator decided to keep key 61689bf468f5 unrevoked, so no revocation lands and `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` is unchanged. Where output or evidence lives: the operator's 2026-11-19 PST decision comment on this ticket.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"74515b93-abb2-4f5a-839e-f0eb79c438b1","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["identity","opcert","operator-decision"],"ticket_id":"9586-0118-310a-4f63","ticket_type":"task","title":"Operator decision: revoke rotated-out op-cert key 61689bf468f5 in trusted_environments.yaml","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f5e30782-4c5a-4467-85f1-528ed07788d5","23b19ed5-8d4f-43bc-9ff1-e8fa1ec4090a","e70028f2-41c7-42e7-85ed-13f5f8a5a868","0e1ed7ce-ab93-4e4b-bc17-314636a43aaa","5dd3687c-55c9-4c79-8972-d157d25756ef","a1022211-71bb-463f-8e2c-bfcd8a4da55d","4d0fdc59-ca16-4231-9dae-c03366224793","69f48bea-77da-44eb-803c-7e3af4794e6d","454863ee-e5a6-4808-80ac-3a896c2fedf8","395cdf81-360e-4780-85ab-1792443e5a21","74515b93-abb2-4f5a-839e-f0eb79c438b1","ea5fd751-f993-4fd8-aa91-38aa45c66c15"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795378532230826